description:
GATES-FIRST bead — implement EARLY, right after the thaw. Codify the known deficiencies as RED/failing gates that the modeling beads (.2-.10) then turn green. Layer on top of the still-green legacy gates (reproducible importer, source coverage 0, region ledger 0, suspicious records 0, hidden/control bytes 0). New gates in packages/core/src/rules/srdAudit.ts + tests, each expected to fail against the CURRENT thawed pack:
  (3) all class levels typed — no raw no-ref feature markers except typed subclass slots, no null numeric spellcasting placeholders (Ranger spellsKnown:null);
  (4) all level-up rows classifiable/applicable;
  (5) no missing feature headings (Rogue Thieves' Cant-style);
  (6) no mixed mechanical note tokens (Druid metal restriction);
  (7) feature/rule/spell/magic-item table links complete;
  (8) no duplicate table linearization in primary prose unless under sourceText;
  (9) choice coverage — every level-1/level-up player choice structured or explicitly out-of-scope with a named unsupported marker;
  (extra) no consumer overlay required for core character creation (ASIs, languages, spellcasting ability/prep, starting equipment present in pack).
Gates must fail loudly in CI. Writing them first makes the deficiencies machine-checkable so .2-.10 have an objective definition of done.
